    "background_story": "Aries was a rare and majestic songbird known for his enchanting trilling melodies. Native to the lush rainforests of South America, he spent his days flitting between the vibrant flowers and trees, filling the air with his euphoric songs. Aries' trilling was unlike anything anyone had ever heard before - a mesmerizing blend of whistles, chirps, and warbles that seemed to capture the very essence of the forest. His music had a profound effect on the other creatures, drawing in a loyal following of birds, monkeys, and even the occasional curious human. As the sun set, Aries would take to the skies, his trilling growing louder and more complex, a symphony of sound that echoed through the forest, a true marvel of nature.",
